   "cumleler": [
    "In earlier lessons we did routine tympanometry with a single probe tone, at two hundred twenty six hertz.",
    "At this frequency the adult middle ear is stiffness dominated, so changes in mass often stay hidden.",
    "Multifrequency tympanometry repeats the same measurement at many probe tone frequencies.",
    "The aim is to find the point where the middle ear moves from stiffness dominated to mass dominated behavior: the resonant frequency.",
    "At the resonant frequency, the effects of mass and stiffness cancel each other; net reactance is zero.",
    "Disorders change mass or stiffness and so shift the resonant frequency; multifrequency measurement reveals this shift."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bilesenler",
   "tur": "ikonlar",
   "bolum_no": "PART 1",
   "bolum": "Why many frequencies?",
   "baslik": "The *components* of admittance",
   "ogeler": [
    {
     "ikon": "grafik",
