     "metin": "B crosses zero",
     "cumle": 3
    },
    {
     "ikon": "tablo",
     "baslik": "Phase angle",
     "metin": "90 with stiffness, 0 at resonance",
     "cumle": 5
    }
   ],
   "cumleler": [
    "In multifrequency measurement, admittance is examined not as a single number but through its two components.",
    "Susceptance, or B, is the component of admittance related to mass and stiffness.",
    "Conductance, or G, is the component related to friction, that is, to the absorption of energy.",
    "Susceptance is positive in the stiffness dominated region and negative in the mass dominated region; it crosses zero at resonance.",
    "Some devices show the magnitude and phase angle of admittance instead of its components; both carry the same information.",
    "In a stiffness dominated system the phase angle is close to plus ninety degrees; at resonance it is zero."
   ]
  },
