   "cumleler": [
    "The hardware is the same as in routine tympanometry: a probe with a speaker, a microphone and a pump.",
    "The difference is that the probe speaker can produce not only two hundred twenty six hertz but many frequencies, up to about two kilohertz.",
    "The ear canal must be sealed airtight; a leak spoils the measurement, especially at low frequencies.",
    "At high frequencies the ear canal no longer behaves like a simple volume of air, so device calibration and corrections matter.",
    "This measurement is not available in every clinic; it is usually done as an additional diagnostic test."
