   "cumleler": [
    "Multifrequency tympanometry is done with two main methods.",
    "In the sweep frequency method, pressure is held constant and the probe tone frequency is swept over a wide range.",
    "The measurement is made first at plus two hundred decapascals, then at tympanometric peak pressure, and the difference is calculated.",
    "At plus two hundred decapascals the drum is tensed and the middle ear contributes least, so the difference gives the middle ear value.",
    "In the sweep pressure method, pressure is swept as in standard tympanometry, and this is repeated at many probe tones in turn.",
    "In both methods, the resonant frequency is the frequency where middle ear susceptance is zero.",
    "The two methods can give different values, so the result is compared with norms for the method used."
