    "As the probe tone frequency rises, the shape of the tympanogram also changes.",
    "At two hundred twenty six hertz, the susceptance and conductance curves have a single peak.",
    "At higher frequencies, especially near resonance, a notch appears at the peak of the susceptance curve.",
    "Six hundred seventy eight hertz is three times two hundred twenty six and is often used as a second probe tone.",
    {
     "yazi": "Notched curves are named by their number of peaks and troughs, such as 1B1G, 3B1G, 3B3G and 5B3G.",
     "ses": "Notched curves are named by their number of peaks and troughs, such as one B one G, three B one G, three B three G and five B three G."
    },
    {
     "yazi": "This classification is based on the model proposed by Vanhuyse and colleagues in 1975.",
     "ses": "This classification is based on the model proposed by Vanhuyse and colleagues in nineteen seventy five."
    },
    "A notch can also appear at six hundred seventy eight hertz in a normal adult ear, but the number and width of notches are limited.",
    "If there are too many notches or a notch is wide, increased mass effect is suspected, such as a flaccid drum or ossicular discontinuity."
